-> ABOUT [node:73fb6132-40d3-4e2d-8b88-334442c4bfa7] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:09.425394+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:55:56.142557+00:00
-> CONTRADICTS [node:ee768ade-394d-475c-92fb-e5c5b28e0efc] @ 2026-09-08T09:55:56.142557+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:ee768ade-394d-475c-92fb-e5c5b28e0efc] @ 2026-09-08T10:09:26.371475+00:00

The monospace face is Source Code Pro, self-hosted as woff2 from the LAN backend at weights 400/500/600, replacing both the Courier New placeholder in the accepted wireframes and the IBM Plex Mono the design system had proposed. It was drawn for code read on screen - dotted zero, a 1 with a full base serif against a tailed l and a serifed I, Latin Extended-A so Polish diacritics are real glyphs - and it is SIL OFL, so self-hosting is unencumbered. Its x-height is 0.486 em against Plex Mono's 0.516, so every arcminute figure in the viewing-distance table drops about 6 percent; the 20px body rule survives with margin and the 16px label size now clears the 5 arcmin comfort floor at 1 m only barely, which argues for the 20px rule rather than against the face.
---
