-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T14:55:08.165705+00:00

Faza 0 is sliced walking-skeleton-first rather than scaffold-first. A slice that delivers only the repo layout, or only the schema, is unverifiable until the last slice lands, which leaves the whole phase without feedback while it is still cheap to change. So slice 1 cuts a thin path through every layer at once - build target, server, one custom element, real tokens, CI - and everything after it hangs off a thing that already runs. Secrets-and-errors and Storybook are genuinely headless because they are verifiable by command with no surface and no argument; the persistence and Service Worker slices each turn on an architectural decision with real alternatives, so both will want to be argued with and neither can run unattended.
---
