created_at: 2026-09-08T15:18:34.795407+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:c3dc31be-39b3-4422-a4f6-41136bfb48aa] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:34.795407+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:34.795407+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:f29aa338-eddb-456b-97ad-00b602cb9a42] @ 2026-09-08T15:18:34.795407+00:00

Redaction is proven on the wire, not in a unit test. A scrubber that works but is never called is worse than no scrubber, because it makes everyone confident - so the test drives the real Sentry client with a transport that captures the envelope on its way out, and asserts on the bytes that would have reached GlitchTip. It also asserts the error message survives: a redactor that passes by destroying the evidence has not passed.
---
