-> DEPENDS_ON [node:a815b136-0de2-49af-ac42-6192c12def24] @ 2026-09-08T15:29:16.492358+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:be297a51-6cb1-4526-bdb5-c01badf562a2] @ 2026-09-08T15:29:05.636131+00:00

Drizzle over better-sqlite3 is the data access layer, chosen from the three candidates the plan named. It is TypeScript-first so the row types are inferred from the schema rather than hand-maintained, and drizzle-kit generates migrations by diffing the schema file, which means the schema is the source of truth instead of a description of one. The alternative worth naming is Kysely, a query builder with equally good typing and less machinery - it was passed over because it has no migration story of its own, and migrations were half of what this layer had to deliver.
